{"id": "curve-easing-family", "name": "Curve and easing maths", "family": "math", "subfamily": "curve-easing", "plain": "Remap a value through a named or written curve, usually for schedules. WAS maps a list through named easings between ranges. SV parses curves with a regex-based interpreter, with no eval. AKatz takes a Python expression through builtins-free eval. Sigma-curve editors (NKD Sigmas Curve, Olm CurveEditor, ComfyUI_Curves, by name only) are the graphical relatives.", "math": "WAS: y=out_min+(out_max\u2212out_min)\u00b7ease((x\u2212in_min)/(in_max\u2212in_min))\nSV: recursive regex substitution over functions min,max,floor,ceil,round\u2026, then manual operator evaluation\nAKatz: eval(expr) with t, z=end_frame, numpy subset", "props": {"operates_on": "FLOAT, lists", "params": "easing, ranges, clamp; curve string"}, "evidence": [{"where": "WASasquatch__was-node-suite-comfyui/nodes/number/number_easing.py:15", "symbol": "class NumberEasing"}, {"where": "WASasquatch__was-node-suite-comfyui/nodes/number/number_easing.py:8", "symbol": "EASING_NAMES"}, {"where": "SirVeggie__comfyui-sv-nodes/__init__.py:3885", "symbol": "class CurveFromEquation"}, {"where": "akatz-ai__ComfyUI-AKatz-Nodes/modules/easing.py:109", "symbol": "eval(expr"}], "providers": [{"pack": "WASasquatch__was-node-suite-comfyui", "author": "WASasquatch", "licence": "MIT", "kind": "original", "nodes": ["NumberEasing"], "note": "", "verdict": "TRY", "risks": ["installs software at runtime", "runs decoded or dynamic code", "paid or partner API", "patches torch or ComfyUI globally", "downloads models"], "res4lyf": false}, {"pack": "SirVeggie__comfyui-sv-nodes", "author": "SirVeggie", "licence": "none-found", "kind": "original", "nodes": ["SV-CurveFromEquation", "SV-ApplyCurve", "SV-ApplyCurveFromStep"], "note": "", "verdict": "MAYBE", "risks": ["paid or partner API", "patches torch or ComfyUI globally"], "res4lyf": false}, {"pack": "ComfyUI-AKatz-Nodes.disabled", "author": "akatz-ai", "licence": "